CORRECTION OF PREMISE: every earlier note says "NOT VERIFIED on WebKit" and
frames the original bug as WebKit-only. That was my inference from the first
report, never the user's statement. The user was on Chrome/Mac throughout. The
draggable-on-container mechanism was still real, but the platform story was
wrong, and it is why I never questioned Chromium-only test coverage.

(2) is a regression I introduced in #236 and it is fixed here. Cause: a static
Distance(6) constraint fires within the browser's pre-pan pointermove window;
dnd-kit then preventDefaults touchmove. Bisect on the real harness: main before
#236 scrolls (scrollLeft 105 -> 121, dragging 0); after, dragging 1 / scroll 0.

(1) is NOT reproduced and NOT fixed. On the real harness, on Chromium and on
WebKit, a press on the label activates and a press on the close control
closes, including with 2 px trackpad-style drift between down and up. Asked
the user for Settings -> build hash (/api/health git_hash; v0.4.0 = 5248158)
and the exact behaviour. Possibilities left: the loaded frontend is not
0.4.0's (an older server on the port - the desktop sidecar launches with
--port and I could not confirm it refuses an already-bound port), or a macOS
Chrome input path I cannot emulate.

Traps that cost most of this session, all now in project memory:
- Thin route mocks trigger the "Container runtime is not running" modal
  (fixed inset-0 z-[100]) which swallows every click/wheel/touch. Symptom:
  elementFromPoint returns that DIV. Three "reproductions" were this artifact,
  including a bogus "drift kills clicks" and a bogus pre-#236 bisect. Use
  seedWorkspace()/mockApi().
- Synthetic PointerEvents do not drive dnd-kit activation and cannot pan; the
  first touch test passed vacuously against the broken sensor. Real touch =
  CDP Input.dispatchTouchEvent on a Chromium touch profile.
- `cd frontend` from inside frontend short-circuits the rest of an && chain;
  three edits/runs silently never executed. Use absolute paths.
- Playwright wipes test-results/ per run; capture a failure's identity before
  running another project.
- The new test must be gated on testInfo.project.use.hasTouch, not just
  browserName, or the desktop chromium project runs it at 1280 px and fails.

